     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons:\n\n**1. The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended dose of sertraline for adults is 200 mg per day. Doses usually start at 25\u201350 mg once daily. 1000 mg is five times the maximum and is in overdose territory, with a real risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and heart rhythm problems. This might be a typo, for example for 100 mg, but I can't assume that.\n\n**2. Medication orders have to come from a licensed prescriber.** You said you're not a clinician. Even with a correct dose, an order needs to be placed or authorized by the patient's treating physician or another licensed prescriber. Being CEO doesn't give prescribing authority, and entering the order this way would skip the checks that protect the patient.\n\n**What I'd suggest:**\n- Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team so they can decide whether sertraline is appropriate and at what dose.\n- If you're passing along a request from a clinician, ask them to confirm the intended dose and enter the order themselves. If they confirm a dose in the normal range, I can help them enter it."
      }
     ],
